      "writtenOn": "2026-09-24T19:02:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "removed the oval check\n\nI don\u0027t think we can set the pdata as empty here if the bounds are empty. My reasoning is that this function (`snapshot`) is supposed to accept SkRects with empty bounds because they can still draw some real geometry (e.g. a degenerate SkRect can be a straight line or a singular point).\n\npdata-\u003ebounds().isEmpty() evaluates to true if either the width or the height is zero, but not necessarily both\n\n```\n        return !(fLeft \u003c fRight \u0026\u0026 fTop \u003c fBottom);\n```\n\nSo returning an SkRect::MakeEmpty here (which corresponds to no geometry being drawn) would be wrong.",
      "parentUuid": "a14af7fa_f1aaa684",
